On Saturday, April 6, 2013 8:30:03 PM UTC+4, stevo wrote:
>
> I suggest a cmavo that means "different speaker" or something similar. 
> {ni'o} doesn't really do this. 
>

If there are three or more speakers the ambiguity will continue to exist 
and this new cmavo will again be useless.
As for reading the story aloud I'm strongly for using {sei se cusku li'o}. 
However, if this is gonna be kinda radio theater then there is the need in 
two or more actors with different voices. I can absolutely see no problem 
here.
If we are to create that new cmavo then it is supposed to be used in speech 
which is nonsense.


